      "writtenOn": "2023-06-02T08:57:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The background behind this change is that I\u0027m implementing a prototype in Chromium to support AVIF hdr images using gain maps, as was done for jpeg, see https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id\u003d1404000\n\nFor this I need to extract the gain map metadata from some xmp, so I\u0027m refactoring SkJpegXmp into a slightly more generic SkXmp. I do need to use it in blink, i.e. outside of Skia, which is why it needs to HAVE SK_API, and ccameron@ suggested putting the header in include/private, as is done with SkjpegMetadataDecoder.h which is also used in blink.\n\nTo be fully transparent this is a prototype and the way in which gain maps and their metadata will be added to avif files has not been finalized and is likely to change. In particular, it probably won\u0027t use xmp, so it\u0027s possible that this change won\u0027t be needed in the long term (at least as far as AVIF is concerned). Therefore if there is a strong reason to avoid making this semi public, we could also reconsider implenting the prototype.",
      "parentUuid": "d45c4fa0_b840abae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 2,
        "endChar": 24
